IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cp60-nouns`

-- Row il-60. THE ONE REFERENCE, as typed values, and its control.
-- A citation is encoded as TWO things: what the citing words name, and what the target is labelled and prints. A test compares the two labels, and a second test asks whether the target, by its own printed last day,
-- still stands on a given day. Where the labels agree and the printed last day has passed, the citation resolves and yet names a paragraph that does not stand; that is the finding, kept in an expected-red file
-- with its count declared in check.sh and encoding.json.
-- THE FINDING: s 220ג(ג) names, in its opening words, paragraph (4) of s 220ד(א); the words of that paragraph end "הוראה זו תעמוד בתוקפה עד יום ו׳ באב התשפ״ה (31 ביולי 2025)".
-- CONTROL: the same sentence of s 220ג(ג) also names subsection (ב) of the same section; the words of subsection (ב), as printed, give no day.
-- LIMBS. Limb (a) is the question whether the target is as the citing words say it is; limb (b) is the question whether the citing words still read so in the latest official text of the citing provision.
-- Each limb says where it was read from (see `Where a reading comes from` in cp60-nouns.l4). The Hebrew Wikisource text is not official.
-- A date for which the sources held give no answer is NOTHING; there is no REFUSE.

§ `Cross-references`

GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the citing words name what the target is labelled` MEANS c's `the citing words name` EQUALS c's `the target is labelled`

GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the citation resolves in the official text read` MEANS
    `the citing words name what the target is labelled` c
    AND c's `the target exists in the official text read`

GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the target prints a last day` MEANS NOT (c's `the last day printed in the target` EQUALS NOTHING)

-- Whether the target stands on a day, by its own printed last day. The words "עד יום ו׳ באב" do not say whether the printed day itself is within the period (fork E1 in NOTES.md), and this row reads no day on which the target began.
-- So the only answer the sources held can give is: from the first day that is certainly after the printed day, JUST FALSE; on the printed day and on every earlier day, and for a target that prints no day, NOTHING.
GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the target stands on` MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the first day certainly after the printed day`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST gone THEN IF day AT LEAST gone THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Printed date pairs`

GIVEN p IS A `A printed date pair`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the printed pair matches the routine` MEANS p's `the Gregorian date printed with it` EQUALS p's `the Gregorian date the calendar routine gives`

-- THE CITING WORDS (limb b). Sefer HaChukim 2999 (7 Tammuz 5782, 6 July 2022), printed p. 1017, read from the page image: the words are within section 1 of the instrument printed there under the Hebrew title rendered
-- "Criminal Procedure Law (Amendment No. 92 - Temporary Provision), 5782-2022" (the row's rendering of the Hebrew title, not an enacted title).
-- Its section 220ג(ג) as the page prints it, and as the consolidation prints it (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY for the consolidation's line; the words agree once the wiki marks are removed):
-- ext:[SH 2999 p.1017, read from the page image] | (ג) על אף האמור בסעיף 49 לחוק בתי המשפט, בסעיף קטן (ב) ובסעיף 220ד(א)(4), נשיא בתי המשפט הקהילתיים רשאי להורות, מטעמים מיוחדים שיירשמו
-- src:1326 | (ג) על אף האמור בסעיף 49 לחוק בתי המשפט, בסעיף קטן (ב) ובסעיף 220ד(א)(4), נשיא בתי המשפט הקהילתיים רשאי להורות, מטעמים מיוחדים שיירשמו, כי עניינו של נאשם יהיה נידון בבית משפט קהילתי באותו מחוז אף אם מקום מגוריו של הנאשם אינו באזור שיפוטו או בסמוך אליו.
-- The heading line of the section in the consolidation carries one amendment tag, and no other (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY): the tag is the 2022 instrument's, and no later instrument was read.
-- src:1323 | סעיף 220ג – העברת עניינו של נאשם לדיון בבית משפט קהילתי [תיקון: תשפ״ב־4]
-- THE TARGET (limb a). The same page, paragraph (4) of subsection (א) of s 220ד, read from the page image: the paragraph ends with its own printed last day and the Gregorian date beside it.
-- ext:[SH 2999 p.1017, read from the page image] | (4) הוסמך בית משפט קהילתי באזור השיפוט שמקום מגוריו של הנאשם נמצא בו כאמור בצו לפי סעיף 220יד; הוראה זו תעמוד בתוקפה עד יום ו׳ באב התשפ״ה (31 ביולי 2025);
-- src:1334 | (4) הוסמך בית משפט קהילתי באזור השיפוט שמקום מגוריו של הנאשם נמצא בו כאמור בצו לפי סעיף 220יד; הוראה זו תעמוד בתוקפה עד יום ו׳ באב התשפ״ה (31 ביולי 2025);
-- The heading line of s 220ד in the consolidation carries one amendment tag, and no other (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY): the 2022 instrument's. The consolidation's line for paragraph (4) prints the same day; a later instrument that changed it was not looked for.
-- src:1329 | סעיף 220ד – תנאים להעברת דיון [תיקון: תשפ״ב־4]
-- THE FIRST DAY CERTAINLY AFTER. The printed day is 31 July 2025 (6 Av 5785, see the date pairs below). Whether "until the day" takes the day in or leaves it out is not settled by the words (fork E1), so the row records 1 August 2025, the day after it,
-- as the first day that is certainly past it on either reading. This is the row's own reading of the words, not a quotation.
`reference: s 220ג(ג) to paragraph (4) of s 220ד(א)` MEANS
    `A cross-reference` WITH
        `the citing words are in` IS "Criminal Procedure Law [Consolidated Version], s 220ג(ג), the words 'ובסעיף 220ד(א)(4)', as printed on p. 1017 of Sefer HaChukim 2999, within section 1 of the instrument"
        `the citing words name` IS "220ד(א)(4)"
        `the target is labelled` IS "220ד(א)(4)"
        `the target exists in the official text read` IS TRUE
        `the last day printed in the target` IS JUST (Date 31 7 2025)
        `the first day certainly after the printed day` IS JUST (Date 1 8 2025)
        `limb (a) was read from` IS `the official instrument, read from its page image; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
        `limb (b) was read from` IS `the official instrument, read from its page image; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`

-- THE CONTROL. The same sentence of s 220ג(ג) names "סעיף קטן (ב)", subsection (ב) of the same section. The subsection starts at the foot of printed p. 1016 and ends at the head of printed p. 1017, and was read from both page images:
-- it prints no day. Its words, in the two parts the pages divide them into:
-- ext:[SH 2999 p.1016, read from the page image] | (ב) על אף האמור בסעיף 49 לחוק בתי המשפט, שופט בית משפט שלום רשאי להורות כי עניינו של נאשם יהיה נידון בבית משפט שלום אחר באותו מחוז שיפוט שהוסמך כבית
-- ext:[SH 2999 p.1017, read from the page image] | משפט קהילתי ושמקום מגוריו של הנאשם הוא באזור שיפוטו או בסמוך אליו, ובלבד שקיבל לכך את אישורו של נשיא בית משפט השלום שבאותו מחוז או של סגן נשיא בית משפט השלום שהוא הסמיך לכך.
-- That the subsection prints no day is a statement about the words just quoted and about nothing outside them.
`reference: s 220ג(ג) to subsection (ב) of s 220ג` MEANS
    `A cross-reference` WITH
        `the citing words are in` IS "Criminal Procedure Law [Consolidated Version], s 220ג(ג), the words 'בסעיף קטן (ב)', as printed on p. 1017 of Sefer HaChukim 2999, within section 1 of the instrument"
        `the citing words name` IS "220ג(ב)"
        `the target is labelled` IS "220ג(ב)"
        `the target exists in the official text read` IS TRUE
        `the last day printed in the target` IS NOTHING
        `the first day certainly after the printed day` IS NOTHING
        `limb (a) was read from` IS `the official instrument, read from its page image; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
        `limb (b) was read from` IS `the official instrument, read from its page image; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`

-- THE DATE PAIRS. Each Hebrew date below was converted with the Hebrew-calendar routine in tools/hebcal.py (tools/datepairs.py runs the conversions and the routine's own control, 30 Kislev 5785 = 31 December 2024, first).
-- THE TARGET'S PAIR, the end of paragraph (4): on the ext line of the target above.
`date pair: the printed end of paragraph (4) of s 220ד(א)` MEANS
    `A printed date pair` WITH
        `the Hebrew date, transliterated` IS "6 Av 5785"
        `the Gregorian date printed with it` IS Date 31 7 2025
        `the Gregorian date the calendar routine gives` IS Date 31 7 2025
        `the pair was read from` IS `the official instrument, read from its page image`

-- THE CONTROL PAIR: the issue date in the footer of the same printed page, 1017.
-- ext:[SH 2999 p.1017, read from the page image; text layer not checked: the footer's is garbled] | ספר החוקים 2999, ז׳ בתמוז התשפ״ב, 6.7.2022
`date pair: the issue date in the footer of printed p. 1017` MEANS
    `A printed date pair` WITH
        `the Hebrew date, transliterated` IS "7 Tammuz 5782"
        `the Gregorian date printed with it` IS Date 6 7 2022
        `the Gregorian date the calendar routine gives` IS Date 6 7 2022
        `the pair was read from` IS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
